v0.10.21: simulations persist; Activity panel fills

Two console bugs. One is silent data loss.

1. Every simulation on a base-rate-less forecast was discarded on save

   run_simulation decides "is this a probability?" by asking whether
   the question carries a base_rate:

     if is_probability_forecast {
         self.predicted_probability = results.mean.clamp(0.01, 0.99);
     } else {
         self.predicted_probability = results.mean;   // unclamped
     }

   The else branch is for counts/magnitudes/durations. But the
   default Fermi decomposition emits a multiplier chain —
   strength_factor * conditions * disruption, all centred on 1.0 —
   whose product sits near 1.0 and routinely exceeds it. Observed:
   1.068.

   create_forecast_handler and update_forecast_handler both reject
   outside [0,1] with "predicted_probability must be between 0 and
   1". So the backend write failed on every save, the local snapshot
   still succeeded, the chip said "Saved just now", and reopening
   showed the pre-simulation value.

   The 400 was visible only in the old three-line banner, truncated
   at "Work will not survive c".

   Fix: clamp_wire_probability at the persistence boundary — both
   persist_backend_save and publish_forecast — so no call path can
   reintroduce it. True mean preserved in simulation_results (no
   range constraint) and on the Trajectory tab. Non-finite → 0.5
   rather than propagating, since NaN/inf serialise to JSON null and
   fail deserialisation with a worse error.

   Clamping emits an Activity warning explaining that a multiplier
   chain isn't a probability, pointing at the base-rate fix.

   Helper lives in the lib target with 5 tests, including the exact
   production value.

2. Seven of eight cockpits were never observed

   CockpitState can't reach FermiConsole, so it queues intent in
   pending_* fields that only a cx.observe handler drains. That
   observer was registered inline in navigate() and nowhere else,
   while eight sites construct a cockpit: navigate, open_forecast,
   open_workspace_forecast, on_new_forecast, on_reset_cockpit,
   on_import_forecast, import_polymarket_forecast, dashboard hero.

   Seven produced an unobserved cockpit. Everything queued from
   those sessions was dropped: toasts, invite-share modal,
   forecast-list refresh, and since v0.10.17 the Activity mirror and
   panel-open request.

   Pre-existing, not a v0.10.17 regression — invisible because a
   toast that never fires reads as "no news". An empty log and a
   dead button don't. The banner's Activity pill is the clearest
   case: sets pending_open_activity, calls notify, nothing drains
   it, no error.

   Fix: install_cockpit() owns adoption AND observation together.
   All eight sites route through it; the only direct assignment to
   self.cockpit is inside it.

Validation:
  cargo test -p fermi-console --lib   18/18
  cargo test -p fermi-activity        18/18
  cargo check --workspace              0 errors

Related:
  v0.10.17  the Activity panel these fixes make usable
  v0.10.18  the lib target that makes the clamp testable at all
